IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Taxation Administration Act 1953 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- how I challenge a tax decision, what penalties can fall on me,
-- and what the Act asks of my private ancillary fund: objections and review (Part IVC: ss 14ZU, 14ZW, 14ZX, 14ZY, 14ZYA, 14ZZ,
-- 14ZZC, 14ZZM, 14ZZN); administrative penalties for false or misleading statements (Schedule 1 ss 284-75, 284-85, 284-90,
-- 284-220, 284-225) and for lodging late (ss 286-75, 286-80); remission and objection (s 298-20); private ancillary funds
-- (Subdivision 426-D: ss 426-105, 426-110, 426-120, 426-125).
--
-- SEAT: the taxpayer -- the individual who objects, who may be penalised, and (in Daniel's life) the founder of a private
-- ancillary fund and director of its trustee company. "Can I challenge this, by when, and what can I be made to pay?" The
-- Commissioner's decisions and satisfactions are asked as facts or answered conditionally.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 226, compilation date 27 August 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 79, 2026 and Act No. 82,
-- 2026), register id C2026C00393, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1953A00001.txt. THE s 284-85(2) FORMULA IS
-- MISSING FROM THE DEPOSIT ("use this formula:" goes straight to "where:"); the penalty after increase and reduction is an
-- INFERENCE from the defined terms (BPA, increase %, reduction %). The value of a penalty unit is Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA ("$330
-- (subject to indexation under subsection (3))", Compilation No. 167, 27 August 2026, register id C2026C00368,
-- ../../../crimes-act-1914/registers/source-bundle/C1914A00012.txt); the indexed value is published by notifiable instrument,
-- so it is an INPUT. The Taxation Administration (Private Ancillary Fund) Guidelines 2019 are NOT DEPOSITED: the minimum annual
-- distribution, the responsible person requirement and the guideline penalty amount are not encoded.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Which assessments have the 2-year period of review (Income Tax Assessment Act 1936 s 170(1) items 1 to 3A -- a
-- borrowed term, asked as a fact); amended assessments (ss 14ZV, 14ZW(1B), (1BA)); private rulings and the other special
-- objection periods of s 14ZW(1); ART procedure beyond the time limit; scheme penalties (s 284-160), the reasonably arguable
-- position (items 4 to 6A of s 284-90(1)), the significant global entity multipliers, s 284-224; the shortfall interest charge
-- (Division 280); the Commissioner's remission (s 298-20(1)) itself; public ancillary funds and community charity trusts; acting
-- trustees (ss 426-130 to 426-165).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Taxation Administration Act 1953 -- objections, penalties, ancillary funds`

§§ `ss 14ZU, 14ZW -- by when must I object`

-- s 14ZU: "A person making a taxation objection must: (a) make it in the approved form; and (b) lodge it with the Commissioner
-- within the period set out in section 14ZW; and (c) state in it, fully and in detail, the grounds that the person relies on."
-- s 14ZW(1)(aa): against an income tax assessment, "(i) if item 1, 2, 3 or 3A of the table in subsection 170(1) of [the Income Tax
-- Assessment Act 1936] applies to the assessment concerned--2 years after notice of the assessment is given to the person; or (ii)
-- otherwise--4 years after notice of the assessment concerned is given". (1BB): against a Division 284 penalty that "relates to an
-- assessment of the person", if the person has longer than 60 days to object against that assessment, "within that longer
-- period". (c): "in any other case--60 days after notice of the taxation decision to which it relates has been served on the
-- person" -- for example a refusal to remit a penalty (s 298-20(3)) or the suspension or removal of a fund's trustee (s
-- 426-125(8)).
DECLARE `What I object to` IS ONE OF
    `my income tax assessment`
    `a Division 284 penalty relating to my income tax assessment`
    `another taxation decision`

DECLARE `My objection` HAS
    `what I object to` IS A `What I object to`
    `the day I was given notice of the decision` IS A DATE
    `the day I was given notice of my income tax assessment` IS A DATE
    `the 2-year period of review applies to my assessment` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day notice of the assessment was given, ISO 8601
      `short period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the 2-year period of review applies
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the assessment objection period` MEANS
    IF `short period` THEN `add years` `the notice` 2 ELSE `add years` `the notice` 4

@export By when must I lodge my taxation objection (s 14ZW(1)(aa), (1BB), (c))?
GIVEN `the objection` IS A `My objection` @desc What you object to, and when you were given notice of it
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I object` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the objection`'s `what I object to`
    WHEN `my income tax assessment` THEN
        `the end of the assessment objection period` (`the objection`'s `the day I was given notice of the decision`)
                                                     (`the objection`'s `the 2-year period of review applies to my assessment`)
    WHEN `a Division 284 penalty relating to my income tax assessment` THEN
        IF `longer` AT LEAST `sixty days` THEN `longer` ELSE `sixty days`
    OTHERWISE `sixty days`
    WHERE
        `sixty days` MEANS `the objection`'s `the day I was given notice of the decision` PLUS 60
        `longer` MEANS `the end of the assessment objection period` (`the objection`'s `the day I was given notice of my income tax assessment`)
                                                                    (`the objection`'s `the 2-year period of review applies to my assessment`)

-- s 14ZW(2): if the period has passed, "the person may nevertheless lodge the objection with the Commissioner together with a
-- written request asking the Commissioner to deal with the objection as if it had been lodged within that period"; (3) the request
-- must state the reasons fully and in detail. s 14ZX(3): if the Commissioner agrees, the objection "is taken to have been lodged
-- with the Commissioner within the required period"; (4): if refused, "the person may apply to the Tribunal for review". The
-- Commissioner's decision is the Commissioner's: answered conditionally.
@export Is my objection treated as lodged in time (ss 14ZW(2), 14ZX)?
GIVEN `the day I lodged it` IS A DATE @desc The day you lodged your objection, ISO 8601
      `the last day to lodge it` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period under s 14ZW
      `I lodged a written extension request with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lodged a written request, with reasons, to have it treated as lodged in time
      `the Commissioner agreed to the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner agreed to the request (if refused, you may apply to the ART)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my objection in time` IF
        `the day I lodged it` AT MOST `the last day to lodge it`
    OR  (`I lodged a written extension request with it` AND `the Commissioner agreed to the request`)

§§ `ss 14ZY, 14ZYA -- making the Commissioner decide`

-- s 14ZYA(1): applies if the Commissioner "has not made an objection decision by whichever is the later of": (a) the end of 60 days
-- after the later of the day the objection is lodged and the day the Commissioner agrees to an extension request; (b) if the
-- Commissioner, by notice served within that original 60-day period, requires information, "the end of the period of 60 days after
-- the Commissioner receives that information". (2): "The person may give the Commissioner a written notice requiring the
-- Commissioner to make an objection decision." (3): if no decision "by the end of the period of 60 days after being given the
-- notice", the Commissioner "is taken to have made a decision under subsection 14ZY(1) to disallow the taxation objection".
@export When does the Commissioner's time to decide my objection run out, so that I may require a decision (s 14ZYA(1))?
GIVEN `the day I lodged it` IS A DATE @desc The day you lodged your objection, ISO 8601
      `the day the Commissioner agreed to an extension` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commissioner agreed to treat a late objection as in time (the lodgement day if none)
      `the Commissioner asked me for information in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner, within the original 60 days, served notice requiring information
      `the day the Commissioner received it` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commissioner received that information (ignored if none was asked)
GIVETH A DATE
`When may I require a decision on my objection` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner asked me for information in time` AND `info` GREATER THAN `original`
    THEN `info` ELSE `original`
    WHERE
        `start` MEANS IF `the day the Commissioner agreed to an extension` GREATER THAN `the day I lodged it`
                      THEN `the day the Commissioner agreed to an extension` ELSE `the day I lodged it`
        `original` MEANS `start` PLUS 60
        `info` MEANS `the day the Commissioner received it` PLUS 60

@export On what day is my objection taken to be disallowed if the Commissioner still has not decided it (s 14ZYA(3))?
GIVEN `the day I gave the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the Commissioner written notice requiring a decision, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`When is my objection taken to be disallowed` MEANS
    `the day I gave the notice` PLUS 60

§§ `ss 14ZZ, 14ZZC, 14ZZM, 14ZZN -- review or appeal, and paying meanwhile`

-- s 14ZZ(1): if dissatisfied with the objection decision, the person may "(a) if the decision is a reviewable objection decision
-- --either: (i) apply to the Tribunal for review of the decision; or (ii) appeal to the Federal Court against the decision; or (b)
-- otherwise--appeal to the Federal Court". s 14ZQ: a reviewable objection decision is "an objection decision that is not an
-- ineligible income tax remission decision" (s 14ZS, former additional tax under the 1936 Act -- asked as a fact).
@export May I apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal against the objection decision, rather than only appeal to the Federal Court (s 14ZZ)?
GIVEN `it is an ineligible income tax remission decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision is about remitting former additional tax under the 1936 Act (s 14ZS)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I go to the ART` IF
    NOT `it is an ineligible income tax remission decision`

-- s 14ZZC(1): an application to the ART "must be made within 60 days after the person making the application is served with notice
-- of the decision" (the ART may extend it: ART Act s 19). s 14ZZN: an appeal to the Federal Court "must be lodged with the Court
-- within 60 days after the person appealing is served with notice of the decision."
@export By when must I apply to the ART or appeal to the Federal Court (ss 14ZZC(1), 14ZZN)?
GIVEN `the day I was served with the objection decision` IS A DATE @desc The day you were served with notice of the objection decision, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I seek review or appeal` MEANS
    `the day I was served with the objection decision` PLUS 60

-- s 14ZZM(1): "The fact that a review is pending in relation to a taxation decision does not in the meantime interfere with, or
-- affect, the decision and any tax, additional tax or other amount may be recovered as if no review were pending." (2): for a
-- small business taxation assessment decision, subject to an ART order under s 32(2) of the ART Act. (s 14ZZR is the same for an
-- appeal, without the exception.)
@export Can the tax be recovered from me while my ART review is pending (s 14ZZM)?
GIVEN `it is a small business taxation assessment decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision assesses liabilities from carrying on a business as a small business entity
      `the ART has made an order staying it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the ART has made an order under s 32(2) of the ART Act affecting the decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the tax be recovered from me meanwhile` IF
    NOT (`it is a small business taxation assessment decision` AND `the ART has made an order staying it`)

§§ `ss 284-75, 284-90 -- a penalty for a false or misleading statement`

-- s 284-75(1): "You are liable to an administrative penalty if: (a) you make a statement to the Commissioner ...; and (b) the
-- statement is false or misleading in a material particular". (5): not liable "if you, and your agent (if relevant), took
-- reasonable care in connection with the making of the statement." (6): not liable if you engage a registered tax agent or BAS
-- agent, give the agent "all relevant taxation information", the agent makes the statement, and its false or misleading nature did
-- not result from the agent's intentional disregard of, or recklessness as to, a taxation law.
DECLARE `My statement` HAS
    `it is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my agent and I took reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a registered tax agent made it for me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I gave the agent all relevant taxation information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent was intentionally disregardful or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Am I liable to a penalty for a false or misleading statement to the Commissioner (s 284-75(1), (5), (6))?
GIVEN `the statement` IS A `My statement` @desc The statement made to the Commissioner, by you or your agent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable for a false or misleading statement` IF
        `the statement`'s `it is false or misleading in a material particular`
    AND (NOT `the statement`'s `my agent and I took reasonable care`)
    AND (NOT (    `the statement`'s `a registered tax agent made it for me`
              AND `the statement`'s `I gave the agent all relevant taxation information`
              AND (NOT `the statement`'s `the agent was intentionally disregardful or reckless`)))

-- s 284-90(1) table: with a shortfall amount, item 1 "intentional disregard" -- "75% of your shortfall amount"; item 2
-- "recklessness" -- 50%; item 3 "a failure ... to take reasonable care" -- 25%. With no shortfall amount: item 3A -- "60 penalty
-- units"; 3B -- 40; 3C -- 20.
DECLARE `How the statement came to be wrong` IS ONE OF
    `intentional disregard of a taxation law`
    `recklessness as to a taxation law`
    `a failure to take reasonable care`

@export What is my base penalty amount for a false or misleading statement (s 284-90(1) items 1 to 3C)?
GIVEN `the cause` IS A `How the statement came to be wrong` @desc Whether it came from intentional disregard, recklessness or a failure to take reasonable care
      `my shortfall amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The shortfall the statement caused, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of a penalty unit (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA, indexed), in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my base penalty amount` MEANS
    IF `my shortfall amount` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `my shortfall amount` TIMES (CONSIDER `the cause`
                                      WHEN `intentional disregard of a taxation law` THEN 75
                                      WHEN `recklessness as to a taxation law` THEN 50
                                      OTHERWISE 25) DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE `the penalty unit` TIMES (CONSIDER `the cause`
                                   WHEN `intentional disregard of a taxation law` THEN 60
                                   WHEN `recklessness as to a taxation law` THEN 40
                                   OTHERWISE 20)

§§ `ss 284-85, 284-220, 284-225 -- the penalty after increases and reductions`

-- s 284-220(1): "The base penalty amount is increased by 20% if: (a) you took steps to prevent or obstruct the Commissioner from
-- finding out about a shortfall amount"; (b) you became aware of it after the statement and "did not tell the Commissioner ...
-- within a reasonable time"; (c), (ca) a base penalty amount was worked out for you under the same group of items previously.
-- s 284-225(2), (3): if "you voluntarily tell the Commissioner, in the approved form, about the shortfall amount ... before ... the
-- day the Commissioner tells you that an examination is to be made of your affairs", the base penalty amount is "(a) reduced by
-- 80% if the shortfall amount, or the part of it, is $1,000 or more; or (b) reduced to nil if the shortfall amount ... is less
-- than $1,000"; (4A): for a statement with no shortfall, "reduced to nil". (1): after being told of an examination, reduced by 20%
-- if telling the Commissioner "can reasonably be estimated to have saved the Commissioner a significant amount of time or
-- significant resources". (5), the Commissioner's discretion to treat a later disclosure as earlier, is an input: answer "before".
DECLARE `What I did about it` HAS
    `I obstructed the Commissioner or did not tell in reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I had a base penalty under the same items before` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I told the Commissioner voluntarily before an examination was notified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I told the Commissioner after an examination was notified, saving significant time` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 284-85(1): if the base penalty amount is neither increased nor reduced, "this is the amount of the penalty". (2): "Otherwise,
-- use this formula:" -- MISSING FROM THE DEPOSIT. INFERENCE from its defined terms ("BPA is the base penalty amount", "increase % is
-- the percentage increase", "reduction % is the percentage reduction"): BPA + (BPA x increase %) - (BPA x reduction %).
@export What penalty must I pay for a false or misleading statement, after increases and reductions (ss 284-85, 284-220, 284-225)?
GIVEN `the base penalty amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Your base penalty amount under s 284-90, in dollars
      `my shortfall amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The shortfall amount, in dollars (0 if none)
      `what I did` IS A `What I did about it` @desc Whether you obstructed, had an earlier penalty, or told the Commissioner, and when
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What penalty must I pay for my statement` MEANS
    `the base penalty amount` PLUS `the base penalty amount` TIMES `increase` DIVIDED BY 100
                              MINUS `the base penalty amount` TIMES `reduction` DIVIDED BY 100
    WHERE
        `increase` MEANS
            IF `what I did`'s `I obstructed the Commissioner or did not tell in reasonable time`
               OR `what I did`'s `I had a base penalty under the same items before`
            THEN 20 ELSE 0
        `reduction` MEANS
            IF `what I did`'s `I told the Commissioner voluntarily before an examination was notified`
            THEN IF `my shortfall amount` AT LEAST 1000 THEN 80 ELSE 100
            ELSE IF `what I did`'s `I told the Commissioner after an examination was notified, saving significant time` THEN 20 ELSE 0

§§ `ss 286-75, 286-80 -- a penalty for lodging late`

-- s 286-75(1): liable if required "to give a return, notice, statement or other document to the Commissioner in the approved form
-- by a particular day" and you do not. (1A): not if you engaged a registered tax agent or BAS agent, gave it all relevant
-- information in time, and its failure did not result from its intentional disregard or recklessness.
-- s 286-80(2)(a): "1 penalty unit for each period of 28 days or part of a period of 28 days starting on the day when the document
-- is due and ending when you give it (up to a maximum of 5 penalty units)". Example: "An entity lodges a return 31 days late. The
-- base penalty amount under subsection (2) is 2 penalty units." (3): multiplied by 2 for a medium withholder, or assessable income
-- or current GST turnover "more than $1 million but less than $20 million"; (4): by 5 for a large withholder, or $20 million or
-- more. (5): the penalty unit is "the amount applying at the start of the relevant 28 day period" -- one value is used here.
DECLARE `My size for s 286-80` IS ONE OF
    `small`
    `medium -- over 1 million and under 20 million, or a medium withholder`
    `large -- 20 million or more, or a large withholder`

GIVEN `days late` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the due day to the day you lodged
GIVETH A NUMBER
`periods of 28 days or part` MEANS
    IF TRUNC (`days late` DIVIDED BY 28) 0 TIMES 28 LESS THAN `days late`
    THEN TRUNC (`days late` DIVIDED BY 28) 0 PLUS 1
    ELSE TRUNC (`days late` DIVIDED BY 28) 0

@export What penalty must I pay for lodging my return late (ss 286-75, 286-80)?
GIVEN `the day it was due` IS A DATE @desc The day the return or document was due, ISO 8601
      `the day I lodged it` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave it to the Commissioner in the approved form, ISO 8601
      `my size` IS A `My size for s 286-80` @desc Your assessable income, GST turnover or withholder size
      `my registered agent was at fault, not me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a registered agent you gave all information to failed to lodge, without its intentional disregard or recklessness
      `the penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of a penalty unit (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA, indexed), in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What penalty must I pay for lodging late` MEANS
    IF `my registered agent was at fault, not me` OR `the day I lodged it` AT MOST `the day it was due` THEN 0
    ELSE `units` TIMES `multiplier` TIMES `the penalty unit`
    WHERE
        `periods` MEANS `periods of 28 days or part` (Day `the day I lodged it` MINUS Day `the day it was due`)
        `units` MEANS IF `periods` GREATER THAN 5 THEN 5 ELSE `periods`
        `multiplier` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my size`
            WHEN `small` THEN 1
            WHEN `medium -- over 1 million and under 20 million, or a medium withholder` THEN 2
            OTHERWISE 5

§§ `s 298-20 -- objecting to a refusal to remit`

-- s 298-20(1): "The Commissioner may remit all or a part of the penalty." (3): if the Commissioner "refuses to any extent to remit an
-- amount of penalty; and (b) the amount of penalty payable after the refusal is more than 2 penalty units; and (c) the entity is
-- dissatisfied with the decision; the entity may object against the decision in the manner set out in Part IVC."
@export May I object to the Commissioner's refusal to remit my penalty (s 298-20(3))?
GIVEN `the Commissioner refused to remit some or all of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner refused, to any extent, to remit the penalty
      `the penalty left to pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The penalty payable after the refusal, in dollars
      `the penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of a penalty unit (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA, indexed), in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I object to the refusal to remit` IF
    `the Commissioner refused to remit some or all of it` AND `the penalty left to pay` GREATER THAN 2 TIMES `the penalty unit`

§§ `ss 426-105, 426-110 -- is my foundation a private ancillary fund`

-- s 426-105(1): "A trust is a private ancillary fund if: (a) each trustee of the trust is a constitutional corporation; and (b) each
-- trustee has agreed, in the approved form given to the Commissioner, to comply with the rules in the private ancillary fund
-- guidelines, as in force from time to time; and (c) none of the trustees has revoked that agreement". (2): revocation only by
-- giving it to the Commissioner in the approved form. s 426-110: the Minister must make the guidelines, setting the rules a fund
-- must comply with to be or remain a deductible gift recipient, and the s 426-120 penalty amount -- the guidelines are NOT
-- DEPOSITED, so the 5% minimum distribution and the responsible person requirement are not encoded. A change in who owns or
-- directs the trustee company does not, on this text, change whether the trust is a private ancillary fund.
@export Is my foundation a private ancillary fund (s 426-105)?
GIVEN `every trustee is a constitutional corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether each trustee is a constitutional corporation (a trading, financial or foreign corporation)
      `every trustee agreed to comply with the guidelines` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether each trustee has agreed, in the approved form given to the Commissioner, to comply with the private ancillary fund guidelines
      `a trustee has revoked that agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any trustee has revoked that agreement by notice to the Commissioner in the approved form
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my foundation a private ancillary fund` IF
        `every trustee is a constitutional corporation`
    AND `every trustee agreed to comply with the guidelines`
    AND (NOT `a trustee has revoked that agreement`)

§§ `s 426-120 -- am I personally liable as a director of the trustee`

-- s 426-120(1): the persons in (2) are jointly and severally liable to an administrative penalty if "(a) a trustee of an ancillary
-- ... fund holds the fund out as being endorsed, entitled to be endorsed, or entitled to remain endorsed, as a deductible gift
-- recipient; and (b) the fund is not so endorsed or entitled." (2)(b): "each director of each constitutional corporation that is a
-- trustee of the fund, if: (i) any of the penalty cannot reasonably be recovered from the constitutional corporation; and (ii) the
-- constitutional corporation is neither a licensed trustee company ... nor the Public Trustee of a State or Territory." (5): (2)(b)
-- does not apply to a director if "(a) the director was not aware of the holding out ... and it would not have been reasonable to
-- expect the director to have been aware of that holding out; or (b) the director took all reasonable steps to ensure that the
-- holding out ... did not occur; or (c) there were no such steps that the director could have taken." (7): the director bears an
-- evidential burden. (4): "The penalty must not be reimbursed from the fund." The amount is set by the guidelines (s 426-120(3)) --
-- not deposited.
DECLARE `The holding out and my part in it` HAS
    `the trustee held the fund out as a deductible gift recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the fund was so endorsed or entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the penalty cannot reasonably be recovered from the trustee company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trustee company is a licensed trustee company or a Public Trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was unaware, and could not reasonably have been aware, of the holding out` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I took all reasonable steps to stop it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there were no steps I could have taken` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Am I, as a director of my fund's trustee company, personally liable to the ancillary fund penalty (s 426-120(1), (2)(b), (5))?
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `The holding out and my part in it` @desc What the trustee held out, whether it was true, and what you knew and did
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable as a director of the trustee` IF
        `the facts`'s `the trustee held the fund out as a deductible gift recipient`
    AND (NOT `the facts`'s `the fund was so endorsed or entitled`)
    AND `the facts`'s `the penalty cannot reasonably be recovered from the trustee company`
    AND (NOT `the facts`'s `the trustee company is a licensed trustee company or a Public Trustee`)
    AND (NOT `the facts`'s `I was unaware, and could not reasonably have been aware, of the holding out`)
    AND (NOT `the facts`'s `I took all reasonable steps to stop it`)
    AND (NOT `the facts`'s `there were no steps I could have taken`)
